{"availability":"available","full":"rosaboyle/mcp-playground","name":"mcp-playground","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"TypeScript","stars":33,"forks":7,"created":"2025-04-14T03:10:20Z","updated":"2025-05-12T22:26:56Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://trmx.ai/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:50.819Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:50.819Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:50.819Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T16:43:50.819Z","stars":33,"forks":7}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The Postman for MCPs A powerful, open-source desktop tool for exploring, debugging, and monitoring Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers—with built-in LLM integration. Learn more and join our community at trmx.ai.","TRMX MCP Playground is your go-to tool for building, testing, debugging, and monitoring MCP servers. Think of it as \"Postman, but for MCPs.\" It’s designed for developers working with the Model Context Protocol (MCP)—a standard that lets LLMs (Large Language Models) discover and use external tools, resources, and prompts in a consistent way.","We noticed the developer experience for MCP was broken—testing, debugging, and monitoring MCP servers was painful. Our vision is twofold:"],"features":["Stage 1: Build a local MCP playground for developers to easily build, test, debug, and monitor their local MCPs.","Stage 2: Launch a serverless MCP platform so anyone can deploy, scale, and share MCPs without managing infrastructure.","Build Local MCP Server or Remote Serverless MCP? (Medium)","First Release Details (Medium)","MCP Server Debugging: Connect to any MCP server and explore its tools, resources, and prompts."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rosaboyle/mcp-playground/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"be18c29fa438bbcdae6bf95df0a07d19f4904a3f7eaad97544d67fc90f6e1043","extractedAt":"2026-10-09